{"id":"08f4a3081239a349","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-unit-counit.md","title":"Unit and Counit","display":"df-unit-counit — Unit and Counit","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-unit-counit","aliases":["58-df-unit-counit","Unit and Counit"],"display":"df-unit-counit — Unit and Counit","depends_on":["[[../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md]]","[[../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md]]","[[../batch04/58-df-category-data.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-unit-counit"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-unit-counit</span><span>Unit and Counit</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-unit-counit — Unit and Counit"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"dfa5042443233c40\" href=\"?note=dfa5042443233c40\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md\">../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"970e2b8779070da0\" href=\"?note=970e2b8779070da0\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md\">../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"e637becf421e4e61\" href=\"?note=e637becf421e4e61\" title=\"../batch04/58-df-category-data.md\">../batch04/58-df-category-data.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,F,G,\\eta,\\varepsilon,X,Y\\in V\">\\(\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,F,G,\\eta,\\varepsilon,X,Y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S:V^4\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\">\\(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"dfa5042443233c40\" href=\"?note=dfa5042443233c40\" title=\"../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md\">../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"970e2b8779070da0\" href=\"?note=970e2b8779070da0\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md\">../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\land Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\">\\(X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\land Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{id}_Z\">\\(\\mathrm{id}_Z\\)</span> (identity morphism of each object <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Z\">\\(Z\\)</span>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (witness predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}unit\\text{-}counit\\text{-}witness} \\vdash \\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,\\eta,\\varepsilon)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\eta,1_{\\mathcal C},G\\circ F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal C)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\varepsilon,F\\circ G,1_{\\mathcal D},\\mathcal D,\\mathcal D)\\land\\forall X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\;(\\varepsilon_{F(X)}\\circ F(\\eta_X)=\\mathrm{id}_{F(X)})\\land\\forall Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\\;(G(\\varepsilon_Y)\\circ\\eta_{G(Y)}=\\mathrm{id}_{G(Y)})\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}unit\\text{-}counit\\text{-}witness} \\vdash \\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,\\eta,\\varepsilon)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\eta,1_{\\mathcal C},G\\circ F,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal C)\\land\\mathrm{NaturalTransformation}_S(\\varepsilon,F\\circ G,1_{\\mathcal D},\\mathcal D,\\mathcal D)\\land\\forall X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\;(\\varepsilon_{F(X)}\\circ F(\\eta_X)=\\mathrm{id}_{F(X)})\\land\\forall Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\\;(G(\\varepsilon_Y)\\circ\\eta_{G(Y)}=\\mathrm{id}_{G(Y)})\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}unit\\text{-}counit\\text{-}components} \\vdash \\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,\\eta,\\varepsilon)\\land X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\land Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\\to(\\eta_X\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal C}(X,G(F(X)))\\land\\varepsilon_Y\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal D}(F(G(Y)),Y))\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}unit\\text{-}counit\\text{-}components} \\vdash \\operatorname{UnitCounit}_S(F,G,\\mathcal C,\\mathcal D,\\eta,\\varepsilon)\\land X\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal C)\\land Y\\in\\operatorname{Obj}(\\mathcal D)\\to(\\eta_X\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal C}(X,G(F(X)))\\land\\varepsilon_Y\\in\\operatorname{Hom}_{\\mathcal D}(F(G(Y)),Y))\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Unit and counit: natural transformations satisfying triangle identities</li>\n<li>The componentwise triangle identities avoid ambiguous whiskering notation.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-adjunction</code> is the algebraic-geometric adjunction formula and is unrelated to adjoint functors.</li>\n<li>Examples: free/forgetful (unit inserts generators), tensor/hom adjunction</li>\n<li>Monadic: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T = GF\">\\(T = GF\\)</span> monad; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"F \\dashv G\">\\(F \\dashv G\\)</span> monadic if certain conditions hold</li>\n<li>Monoidal categories: dual adjunction gives dual monoidal structure</li>\n<li>The source arities are explicit, and the component conclusion now carries its object-membership guards instead of relying on free contextual choices of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Y\">\\(Y\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Mac Lane, Categories for the Working Mathematician</li>\n<li>Borceux, Handbook of Categorical Algebra</li>\n<li>Riehl, Category Theory in Context</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md","status":"resolved","id":"dfa5042443233c40","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md","status":"resolved","id":"970e2b8779070da0","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-natural-transformation.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch04/58-df-category-data.md","status":"resolved","id":"e637becf421e4e61","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-category-data.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch11/58-df-adjoint-functors.md","status":"reso